"""Generate the evidence table directly from the benchmark runner's measurements."""
import json


def write_report(e, root):
    lines = ['# Why Monad', '', 'Generated by `contracts/bench/run.sh` from production bytecode and cold isolated calls.', '',
        f"Measured at {e['generatedAt']}. Foundry `{e['foundryVersion'].splitlines()[0]}`. Fixed seed: {e['seed']}.", '',
        '## Clearing measurements', '',
        '`clearGas` measures `_clear()` only. It excludes transaction intrinsic gas, the telemetry write, and the event. Costs below convert that measured work at 100 MON-gwei with zero priority fee; the actual billed fee uses the declared transaction limit.', '',
        '| Scenario | Active ticks per side | Orders | Scan width | MonadNine gas | MonadTen gas | Ratio | Nine MON | Ten MON | Nine / Ten share of 150M block |',
        '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for s in e['scenarios']:
        a, b = s['monadNine'], s['monadTen']
        lines.append(f"| {s['name']} | {s['activeTicks']} | {s['orders']} | {s['scanTicks']} | {a:,} | {b:,} | {s['ratio']:.3f}× | {a / 1e7:.7f} | {b / 1e7:.7f} | {a / 1.5e6:.4f}% / {b / 1.5e6:.4f}% |")
    lines += ['', 'Ten orders cannot occupy 32 ticks per side. The order-count experiment instead fixes two occupied ticks (bid 143, ask 112), a 32-tick scan, and 500 lots per side; only the partition into 10, 100, or 1,000 orders changes. The three books have identical clearing results. This resolves an impossible literal reading of the session specification.', '',
        '## Layout ablation under MonadTen', '',
        'The mapping variant is generated mechanically from production source; only the ladder declarations and addressing change. Metadata moves because the arrays become mapping roots. Both layouts use the identical auction algorithm and compare every economic result field.', '',
        '| Active ticks per side | Array gas | Mapping gas | Mapping / array |', '|---|---:|---:|---:|']
    for a in e['ablation']:
        lines.append(f"| {a['activeTicks']} | {a['monadTenContiguous']:,} | {a['monadTenMapping']:,} | {a['ratio']:.3f}× |")
    lines += ['', '## Explicit transaction limits', '',
        'Each limit is `ceil(measuredWorst × 1.075 / 1000) × 1000`. Measurements include callee execution before refunds and exact transaction/calldata intrinsic gas. They cover the demo market parameters, six Mo orders, and claim chunks of at most 50. Sparse tied-price books, fresh tick writes, relayed cancellation, partial claims to distinct owners, claims scattered across historical order/result pages, and self-clearing claims/drips contribute to the maxima. These are measured maxima over the published fixtures, not a formal upper bound over all possible market parameters.', '',
        '| Call | Measured worst gas | Declared limit | Billed MON at minimum base fee | Share of 150M block |', '|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for name, row in e['entrypoints'].items():
        n = row['limit']
        lines.append(f"| {name} | {row['measuredWorst']:,} | {n:,} | {n / 1e7:.7f} | {n / 1.5e6:.4f}% |")
    lines += ['', '## What each Monad behavior changes', '',
        'MIP-8 prices cold storage by 128-slot page. `bidTicks` starts at slot 0 and `askTicks` at slot 256, placing the ladder on exactly four pages. Under MonadNine, reading 512 cold slots costs 512 separate cold reads; under MonadTen, four cold page reads make the remaining ladder reads warm. The measured difference also includes metadata and result writes; the benchmark is an auction, not a bare SLOAD sum. [MIP-8 specification](https://mips.monad.xyz/MIPs/MIP-8), [Monad MIP-8 explanation](https://www.monad.xyz/blog/mip-8).', '',
        f"Gas-limit billing makes a possible self-clear load-bearing for every new order. The measured `placeSelfClear` declared limit is **{e['entrypoints']['placeSelfClear']['limit']:,} gas**. The clients import this bound from `packages/core/src/gas.json`; they cannot choose the smaller no-clear number from the state before inclusion. Gas price remains dynamic. [Monad gas pricing](https://docs.monad.xyz/developer-essentials/gas-pricing). The 7.5% margin comes from [Category Labs' gas-limit analysis](https://www.category.xyz/blogs/setting-your-gas-limit-on-monad); it is guidance, not a protocol guarantee.", '',
        'Approximately 300 ms blocks make a one-block batch roughly 3.3 auctions per second while there is order flow. A sealed batch still needs a transaction to execute clearing; the keeper supplies one during idle periods. Whole-second RPC timestamps cannot establish an exact subsecond median. [Monad deployment summary](https://docs.monad.xyz/developer-essentials/summary).', '',
        'Monad uses local mempools rather than one globally propagated pool. This reduces broad pre-inclusion visibility, but does not prove that validators or RPC operators cannot see or react to pending orders. Batchelor\'s fairness claim instead comes from permutation-invariant allocation after inclusion; no mempool-privacy guarantee is needed. [Monad deployment summary](https://docs.monad.xyz/developer-essentials/summary).', '',
        'The default client orders transactions by descending total gas price. Priority can influence inclusion or ordering, while all accepted orders in the same batch settle at the same clearing price. A limit and the cutoff pro-rata rule determine fills. This does not promise equal quantities or identical entry blocks. [Monad gas pricing](https://docs.monad.xyz/developer-essentials/gas-pricing).', '',
        '## Optimization and correctness', '']
    baseline = e['optimization']['before'].get('MonadTen', {}).get('clear256')
    if baseline:
        lines.append(f"The initial MonadTen full-range clear was {baseline['gas']:,} gas. Profiling identified the tagged ladder copy and uncrossing loops as the two largest costs. Caching the batch tag, bounded memory-safe loops, candidate reuse, and exactly two packed result writes reduce it to {e['optimization']['after']['MonadTen']:,} gas. The 250K target remains unmet; this is reported honestly. The same optimized bytecode is compared across both hardforks. Independent reference, permutation, rounding, and invariant tests remain the correctness gate.")
    lines += ['', f"The runner reproduced every measurement twice exactly. Full-range ratio: **{e['acceptance']['fullRangeRatio']:.3f}×**. Order-count variation: " + ', '.join(f"{k} {v:.2%}" for k, v in e['acceptance']['orderCountVariation'].items()) + '.', '',
        '## Testnet confirmation', '']
    live_path = root / 'contracts/bench/out/clear-live-testnet.json'
    if live_path.exists() and e.get('liveTestnet', {}).get('status') == 'passed':
        live = json.loads(live_path.read_text())
        lines.append(f"Status: **{live['status']}**. {live.get('reason', '')}")
        if 'parity' in live:
            p = live['parity']
            lines.append(f"Local {p['local']:,} gas; live {p['live']:,} gas; difference {p['relativeDifference']:.2%}.")
        for t in live.get('transactions', []):
            lines.append(f"- {t['action']}: [{t['hash']}](https://testnet.monadscan.com/tx/{t['hash']})")
    else:
        lines.append('Pending. Run `pnpm bench:live` with a funded throwaway testnet key. The script verifies chain ID 10143, preflights the entire run, persists transaction hashes, fills 128 ticks per side atomically, triggers a self-clear, and compares emitted `clearGas` to the exact local fixture within 5%. No live number is substituted for a local measurement.')
    lines += ['', 'No mainnet deployment or transaction is part of this session.', '']
    (root / 'docs/WHY_MONAD.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
